{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":381544,"name":"","username":"little_princess","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.ai.google.dev/little_princess/{size}/178877_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:39:49.377Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi Antigravity team,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am a paying Google AI Pro subscriber and want to share concrete feedback regarding the recent update that removed the separate Argon pool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, I appreciate that my weekly limit was reset early after the update. However, the actual consumption rate on the remaining Gemini pool has become drastically worse — to the point where the subscription feels much less usable than before.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere is my exact usage from a single session today:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGoogle Antigravity (Gemini pool): 12 chats total, only 2 of which involved writing large code (the other 10 were very light tasks). Result: \u003cstrong\u003e45% of my weekly quota consumed in one session\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDirect comparison — Claude (Opus 5.5): 8 chats total, 7 of which involved writing massive codebases for video generation. Result: \u003cstrong\u003eonly 23% of my weekly quota consumed\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat makes this especially frustrating is that before this Antigravity update, my Claude weekly limit used to run out faster than Antigravity’s. Now, after removing the Argon pool, the Gemini weekly limit drains at an extreme rate even on light workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am not looking for a refund — I genuinely want to keep using Antigravity. Could the team please investigate whether there is a quota calculation bug after the Argon pool removal, and consider restoring/compensating affected users’ weekly quotas or adjusting the burn rate?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca cla